## 5. Telemetry & Tuning Parameters

Publish these items to NetworkTables for live adjustment on Glass/Elastic and plotting in AdvantageScope:

### Tunable Parameters (Adjustable in Glass/Elastic)

These parameters should be exposed as sliders during elevator tuning.

| Parameter | Widget | Purpose |
|-----------|---------|---------|
| kP | Slider | Position control gain |
| Feedforward kS | Slider | Static friction compensation |
| Feedforward kG | Slider | Gravity compensation |
| Max Velocity | Slider | Maximum elevator velocity |
| Max Acceleration | Slider | Maximum elevator acceleration |
| Position Tolerance | Slider | Allowed position error before reporting "At Setpoint" |
| Upper Soft Limit | Slider | Maximum elevator travel |
| Lower Soft Limit | Slider | Minimum elevator travel |

### Preset Positions

| Parameter | Widget | Purpose |
|-----------|---------|---------|
| Stow Height | Number Input | Elevator stowed position |
| Intake Height | Number Input | Elevator intake position |
| L1 Height | Number Input | Level 1 scoring position |
| L2 Height | Number Input | Level 2 scoring position |
| L3 Height | Number Input | Level 3 scoring position |
| L4 Height | Number Input | Level 4 scoring position (if applicable) |

### Telemetry (Display Only)

These values should always be visible to drivers, programmers, and controls engineers.

| Telemetry Item | Widget | Purpose |
|---------------|---------|---------|
| Current Elevator Position | Numeric Display | Measured elevator position |
| Target Position | Numeric Display | Commanded elevator position |
| Position Error | Numeric Display | Difference between target and actual position |
| Current Elevator Velocity | Numeric Display | Measured elevator speed |
| Motor Output (%) | Gauge | Applied motor output |
| Motor Current (A) | Gauge | Motor current draw |
| Motor Temperature (°C) | Numeric Display | Motor temperature |
| Bottom Limit Switch | Boolean Box | Home switch status |
| Elevator Homed | Boolean Box | Elevator has been zeroed |
| At Setpoint | Boolean Box | Elevator is within tolerance |
| Elevator State | Text Display | STOW, INTAKE, L1, L2, L3, etc. |

### Mechanical Health Monitoring

These diagnostics help identify issues with the cord-driven elevator.

| Diagnostic | Widget | Purpose |
|-----------|---------|---------|
| Motor Current | Gauge | Detects excessive loading or binding |
| Position Error | Numeric Display | Detects inability to reach commanded position |
| Velocity Error | Numeric Display | Detects motion-profile tracking issues |
| Soft Limit Active | Boolean Box | Indicates software travel limits are engaged |
| Limit Switch Active | Boolean Box | Indicates home switch activation |

### Warning Indicators

Monitor these values during testing.

| Symptom | Possible Cause |
|----------|---------------|
| High Motor Current + Increasing Position Error | Cord stretching |
| High Motor Current + Low Velocity | Carriage binding |
| Oscillating Position Error | kP too high or mechanical backlash |
| Large Velocity Error | Motion constraints too aggressive |
| Unexpected Limit Switch Activation | Sensor alignment issue |
| Elevator Stalls Below Setpoint | Insufficient kS or excessive friction |
| Elevator Slowly Drifts Downward | Insufficient kG compensation |
| Sudden Current Spikes | Pulley damage, misalignment, or obstruction |

